<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">About</p>
  <h1>A small team building one thing well.</h1>
  <p class="lead">WebPing is a WhatsApp CRM by Webpeaker, built from Jaipur, Rajasthan. We
  work with small and mid-sized businesses whose customers happen to live on WhatsApp —
  which in India is most of them.</p>
</section>

<section class="section sec-white"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">Our story</p>
    <h2>Built out of a real problem, not a market opportunity.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Before WebPing, we watched small businesses try to run their sales and support
    from a handful of personal phones — one person holding the number, everyone else wondering
    what was promised to which customer.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <h3>Why we started</h3>
      <p>Teams were copying chat threads into notes, forgetting follow-ups, and losing deals not
      because the product was bad but because the conversation had no shared home. Existing tools
      were either heavy enterprise suites priced like them, or cheap wrappers that put your
      customers at risk.</p>
      <p>So we built WebPing: the shared inbox, broadcast engine and deal board a small team
      actually needs, on the official WhatsApp Business Platform — nothing more, nothing less.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Where we are</h3>
      <p>We are a deliberately small team in Jaipur, Rajasthan. Small is a choice: it keeps the
      people who write the code answering your support messages, and it keeps the roadmap honest —
      features get built because customers ask for them, not because a slide deck promised them.</p>
      <div class="stat-row" style="margin-top:22px">
        <div class="stat"><b>1</b><span>number for the whole team</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>2</b><span>plans — Pro and Enterprise</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>1 day</b><span>full-refund window</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section sec-cream"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">What we make</p>
    <h2>One product. Everything it promises, it actually has.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid cols-3">
    <div class="card"><h3>Shared inbox</h3><p>Your business number, answered by the whole team. Assign chats, see who replied what, and never lose a customer inside a colleague's phone again.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Broadcasts</h3><p>Approved message templates sent in paced batches — announcements, reminders and offers that reach real people without hammering the API.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Automations</h3><p>Rules for the routine replies: greetings outside working hours, keyword responses, follow-up nags for chats that go quiet.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Reply drafts</h3><p>AI-assisted drafts grounded in your own documents. A human reviews every draft before it goes out — automation assists, your team decides.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Sales pipelines</h3><p>A deal board attached to the actual chat, so a conversation and its stage of the sale live in the same place.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Dashboard &amp; roles</h3><p>Live response times, per-agent activity, admin-only controls and an audit log — the boring things that keep a team accountable.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section sec-white"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">How we work</p>
    <h2>Promises we can keep, kept in writing.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <h3>What you can expect from us</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li><b>Documentation you can trust.</b> Screenshots taken from the real product, not mockups of an ideal version.</li>
        <li><b>Updates on a schedule.</b> Changes announced before release windows — no silent churn while your team works.</li>
        <li><b>Refunds without a fight.</b> Every new subscription carries a 1-day full refund. If you change your mind, that's it.</li>
        <li><b>Support that answers.</b> A written reply within a business day — from a person, not a ticket queue.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>What we deliberately avoid</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Vanity numbers on this site. If a claim can't be verified by you, it doesn't get written by us.</li>
        <li>Tier confusion. Two plans: Pro and Enterprise. The differences are on one page.</li>
        <li>Talking to your customers for you. Every automated draft is reviewed by a human before it is sent.</li>
        <li>Engagement theatre. If a chat isn't going somewhere, the right move is to follow up or close it cleanly.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>How we handle your data</h3>
      <p>Messages are encrypted in transit and at rest, access is scoped by role, and the audit log
      records who did what. The details are on the <a href="/security">security page</a> — written
      for business owners, not lawyers.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section sec-lav"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">Getting started</p>
    <h2>From sign-up to first broadcast, same day.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step"><b>1. Connect</b><span>Link your official WhatsApp Business number to the inbox.</span></div>
    <div class="step"><b>2. Invite</b><span>Add your team — agents, admins — with the roles they need.</span></div>
    <div class="step"><b>3. Import</b><span>Bring in your contact list with tags and custom fields.</span></div>
    <div class="step"><b>4. Send</b><span>Approve templates, schedule the first broadcast, and watch replies land in the shared inbox.</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

